===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|stellen}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|*stellen}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*stalljan}}.

====Verb====
{{nl-verb}}

# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[position]]; place
# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[state]], to put forward (a question or problem)
#: {{ux|nl|Na het college is er gelegenheid om vragen te '''stellen'''.|There is an opportunity to '''ask''' questions after class.}}
# {{lb|nl|transitive}} to [[suppose]] (commonly as an imperative and followed by a clause beginning with {{m|nl|dat}})
#: {{uxi|nl|'''Stel''' dat iemand je een jaar geleden had verteld dat je weer zou kunnen lachen, had je hem dan geloofd?|'''Suppose''' someone had told you a year ago that you would be able to laugh again, would you have believed him?}}
# {{lb|nl|reflexive}} to take one's stand
# {{lb|nl|transitive|chemistry}} to [[standardize]] a solution by titration

